CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "ccd7b51c-6e50-4e6d-ad9b-1bfbae5c705c",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-21T04:20:55Z",
  "ticket_id": "6add-c1fc",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "The CI pipeline template (examples/ci.example.yml) runs Semgrep OSS instead of Bandit, using a pinned semgrep/semgrep Docker container tag with --metrics=off and --error; SARIF output is written to semgrep-results.sarif and uploaded as a GitHub Actions artifact. SARIF upload to GitHub Security tab (via upload-sarif with continue-on-error: true) includes a jq post-processing step to convert string severity labels to CVSS numerics (workaround for semgrep/semgrep#10834). SARIF upload is best-effort and decoupled from the blocking CI gate.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable CI pipeline configuration and behavior that persists after implementation, not a one-time migration task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "A generate-semgrep-config.sh script produces a .semgrep.yml with mandatory rulesets (p/security-audit, p/owasp-top-ten, p/cwe-top-25) plus stack-specific rulesets mapped from detect-stack.sh output: python-poetry -> p/python; node-npm -> p/javascript; golang -> p/golang; convention-based/unknown -> mandatory rulesets only. The generated config passes semgrep --validate.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability where the script reliably produces validated semgrep configs, not a one-time migration task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "/dso:onboarding calls generate-semgrep-config.sh during CI setup and writes these config keys to dso-config.conf: semgrep.enabled (bool, default true), semgrep.metrics (string, default \"off\"), semgrep.fail_on (string: error|warning, default \"error\"), semgrep.custom_rulesets (comma-separated paths, default empty).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior where onboarding produces config keys that persist in dso-config.conf for ongoing semgrep operation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "The CI step runs semgrep scan --error --severity ERROR (or --severity WARNING --severity ERROR when semgrep.fail_on=warning), causing exit code 1 when findings exist at or above the configured threshold. The PR is blocked via required status check. The blocking gate depends on Semgrep's exit code, not on SARIF upload success.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable CI/CD system behavior where semgrep scanning with specific thresholds blocks PRs via required status checks"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "INSTALL.md and README each contain a Semgrep section covering: Docker prerequisite, the --metrics=off flag and its purpose for government teams, how to add custom rulesets via semgrep.custom_rulesets, and how to change the fail_on threshold.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "documentation updates are one-time tasks to be completed, not durable ongoing system properties"
      },
      "user_decision": "reject",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "**SC (self-use, Probe-1 remediation, architecture-vs-evidence audit 2026-05-16):** During the 6add sprint, `.github/workflows/ci.yml` of the DSO repo itself adopts the new Semgrep gate (mirroring `examples/ci.example.yml`), and at least one sprint PR triggers a successful Semgrep job. Verification (in-session, at sprint Phase I): `grep -n 'semgrep' .github/workflows/ci.yml` returns \u22651 hit referencing the pinned container tag; `gh run list --workflow=ci.yml --branch=<sprint-branch> --json conclusion,jobs | jq '.[].jobs[] | select(.name | test(\"[Ss]emgrep\")) | .conclusion'` shows `success` on at least one sprint run.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes one-time adoption of a gate into CI configuration and verification of a sprint PR run, with specific verification commands indicating completion milestones rather than ongoing system behavior"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    }
  ]
}
